# ============================================================================
#  HONOR FUR-602/603 -- kernel config fragment for ImmortalWrt 25.12.2
# ============================================================================
#  Applied to: target/linux/mediatek/filogic/config-6.12
#
#  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  PART 1 -- WHY THE KERNEL-CONFIG PART IS EMPTY
#  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  There are NO active directives in this file. Every line is a comment.
#
#  Upstream ImmortalWrt/OpenWrt keeps the following OUT of the target kernel
#  config on purpose, and ships them as opt-in kmod packages instead:
#
#    * tc / qdisc / ifb      (NET_SCH_*, NET_CLS_*, IFB, NET_ACT_MIRRED)
#    * netfilter             (NF_TABLES, ...)
#    * mac80211 / mt76       (MAC80211, CFG80211)
#    * USB                   (USB_XHCI_HCD, ...)
#
#  These are exactly the things a QoS/SQM user wants, so the temptation is to
#  force them to =y. DO NOT DO THAT:
#
#    * it bloats the kernel and diverges from upstream, which makes future
#      rebases harder and increases the chance of a boot failure;
#    * it is unnecessary -- the same modules are available as kmod packages
#      built from the identical source tree, so they are ABI-compatible.
#
#  The reference port for this board (hanwckf/immortalwrt-mt798x,
#  target/linux/mediatek/mt7981/config-5.4) takes the same approach.
#
#  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  PART 2 -- WHAT WE ACTUALLY DO INSTEAD
#  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  The build is configured with
#
#      CONFIG_ALL_KMODS=y
#
#  CONFIG_ALL_KMODS is a *tristate* knob: it flips every kmod package from its
#  default `n` to `m`. `m` means "build this package and publish it as an .ipk
#  into bin/targets/mediatek/filogic/packages/", NOT "install it into the
#  image". Only packages forced to `y` (DEFAULT_PACKAGES + our DEVICE_PACKAGES)
#  end up in the rootfs.
#
#  Result: a lean image, plus a complete, ABI-matched kmod set that can be
#  side-loaded later on the device, e.g.
#
#      opkg install kmod-sched-cake kmod-ifb kmod-nft-core
#
#  This is deliberately NOT CONFIG_ALL=y, which would additionally pull in every
#  *application* package and make the image unrecognisable.
#
#  The workflow enforces CONFIG_ALL_KMODS=y and verifies the kmod .ipks were
#  actually produced, so "full kmod build" is proven by artifacts, not by a log
#  line.
#
#  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  RULES FOR FUTURE EDITS
#  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#    * Never blanket-enable symbols here.
#    * Only add a symbol if it is genuinely impossible to express as a kmod, and
#      document the reason inline with the evidence that forced it.
#    * Keep this fragment target-scoped: mediatek has no per-target config-6.12,
#      so filogic/config-6.12 is the highest-priority file kconfig.pl merges for
#      this target. Putting the fragment anywhere else would silently not apply.
